{"resource":{"id":"rust-complete-tutorial","title":"Rust — Complete Tutorial","category":"Programming","difficulty":"Beginner","readingTime":"41 min","pages":63,"lastUpdated":"May 2026","tags":["Programming","Rust","Systems"],"heroImage":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1461749280684-dccba630e2f6?w=1800&q=80","heroSubtitle":"Beginner to advanced Rust — ownership, lifetimes, traits, generics, smart pointers, concurrency, async, Cargo, testing, HTTP, database, deployment."},"toc":[{"id":"objectives","label":"Learning Objectives"},{"id":"s1","label":"1. Setup & Cargo"},{"id":"s2","label":"2. Ownership"},{"id":"s3","label":"3. Borrowing"},{"id":"s4","label":"4. Lifetimes"},{"id":"s5","label":"5. Traits"},{"id":"s6","label":"6. Generics"},{"id":"s7","label":"7. Smart Pointers"},{"id":"s8","label":"8. Collections"},{"id":"s9","label":"9. Iterators & Closures"},{"id":"s10","label":"10. Error Handling"},{"id":"s11","label":"11. Testing"},{"id":"s12","label":"12. Concurrency"},{"id":"s13","label":"13. Async/Await"},{"id":"s14","label":"14. File I/O"},{"id":"s15","label":"15. Networking"},{"id":"s16","label":"16. REST APIs (Axum)"},{"id":"s17","label":"17. Database (sqlx)"},{"id":"s18","label":"18. Macros"},{"id":"s19","label":"19. Unsafe Rust"},{"id":"s20","label":"20. Deployment"},{"id":"summary","label":"Summary"},{"id":"faqs","label":"FAQ"},{"id":"glossary","label":"Glossary"},{"id":"references","label":"References"},{"id":"disclaimer","label":"Disclaimer"}],"related":[{"title":"Rust — Beginner Guide","tag":"Programming","time":"17 min"},{"title":"Rust — Interview Questions","tag":"Programming","time":"35 min"},{"title":"Rust — Practice Questions","tag":"Programming","time":"21 min"}],"html":"<section id=\"objectives\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Learning Objectives</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Learn Rust from scratch to production-ready.</li>\n          <li>Build a REST API with database, tests, and CI.</li>\n          <li>Reason about ownership, lifetimes, and traits fluently.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s1\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">1. Setup &amp; Cargo</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>rustup update stable\ncargo new myapp &amp;&amp; cd myapp\ncargo build &amp;&amp; cargo run &amp;&amp; cargo test</code></pre></div>\n        <p><code>Cargo.toml</code> declares dependencies; <code>Cargo.lock</code> pins versions.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s2\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">2. Ownership</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Move semantics by default. Copy types (integers, bools, small tuples of Copy) implement <code>Copy</code> and are duplicated instead of moved.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s3\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">3. Borrowing</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Rule: any number of shared borrows OR exactly one mutable borrow — never both at once.</p>\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1451187580459-43490279c0fa?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 1 — Ownership/borrow checker flow: move, shared borrow, mutable borrow, drop.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s4\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">4. Lifetimes</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Lifetimes label how long references are valid. Most are elided; annotate when the compiler can't infer.</p>\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>fn longest&lt;&#x27;a&gt;(a: &amp;&#x27;a str, b: &amp;&#x27;a str) -&gt; &amp;&#x27;a str {\n    if a.len() &gt; b.len() { a } else { b }\n}</code></pre></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s5\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">5. Traits</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Shared behaviour — Rust's answer to interfaces. Static dispatch by default (monomorphized), dynamic dispatch via <code>dyn Trait</code>.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s6\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">6. Generics</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>fn largest&lt;T: PartialOrd + Copy&gt;(xs: &amp;[T]) -&gt; T {\n    let mut best = xs[0];\n    for &amp;x in xs { if x &gt; best { best = x; } }\n    best\n}</code></pre></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s7\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">7. Smart Pointers</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <table class=\"w-full border-collapse text-sm\">\n          <thead><tr class=\"border-b\"><th class=\"p-2 text-left\">Type</th><th class=\"p-2 text-left\">Purpose</th></tr></thead>\n          <tbody>\n            <tr class=\"border-b\"><td class=\"p-2\"><code>Box&lt;T&gt;</code></td><td class=\"p-2\">Heap allocation, single owner</td></tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b\"><td class=\"p-2\"><code>Rc&lt;T&gt;</code></td><td class=\"p-2\">Shared ownership, single-threaded</td></tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b\"><td class=\"p-2\"><code>Arc&lt;T&gt;</code></td><td class=\"p-2\">Shared ownership, thread-safe</td></tr>\n            <tr><td class=\"p-2\"><code>RefCell&lt;T&gt;</code></td><td class=\"p-2\">Interior mutability, runtime-checked</td></tr>\n          </tbody>\n        </table>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s8\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">8. Collections</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\"><p><code>Vec</code>, <code>String</code>, <code>HashMap</code>, <code>HashSet</code>, <code>BTreeMap</code>, <code>VecDeque</code>.</p></div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s9\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">9. Iterators &amp; Closures</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>let sum: i32 = (1..=10).filter(|n| n % 2 == 0).sum();</code></pre></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s10\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">10. Error Handling</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p><code>Result&lt;T, E&gt;</code>, <code>?</code> operator, <code>thiserror</code> for library errors, <code>anyhow</code> for applications.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s11\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">11. Testing</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>#[cfg(test)]\nmod tests {\n    #[test] fn adds() { assert_eq!(2 + 2, 4); }\n}</code></pre></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s12\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">12. Concurrency</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p><code>std::thread</code>, <code>Arc&lt;Mutex&lt;T&gt;&gt;</code>, channels via <code>std::sync::mpsc</code> or <code>crossbeam</code>.</p>\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1544197150-b99a580bb7a8?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 2 — Concurrency model: threads share state via Arc+Mutex or communicate via channels.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s13\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">13. Async/Await</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>#[tokio::main]\nasync fn main() -&gt; anyhow::Result&lt;()&gt; {\n    let body = reqwest::get(&quot;https://example.com&quot;).await?.text().await?;\n    println!(&quot;{body}&quot;); Ok(())\n}</code></pre></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s14\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">14. File I/O</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>let contents = std::fs::read_to_string(&quot;input.txt&quot;)?;</code></pre></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s15\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">15. Networking</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\"><p>Async TCP with <code>tokio::net</code>, HTTP with <code>reqwest</code>/<code>hyper</code>.</p></div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s16\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">16. REST APIs with Axum</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>use axum::{routing::get, Router};\n#[tokio::main]\nasync fn main() {\n    let app = Router::new().route(&quot;/&quot;, get(|| async { &quot;hello&quot; }));\n    axum::Server::bind(&amp;&quot;0.0.0.0:3000&quot;.parse().unwrap())\n        .serve(app.into_make_service()).await.unwrap();\n}</code></pre></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s17\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">17. Database with sqlx</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\"><p>Compile-time checked SQL, async, works with Postgres/MySQL/SQLite.</p></div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s18\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">18. Macros</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Declarative (<code>macro_rules!</code>) and procedural (custom derive, attribute, function-like).</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s19\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">19. Unsafe Rust</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-4 rounded-2xl border-l-4 border-red-500/40 bg-red-500/10 text-red-900 dark:text-red-100 p-4\"><div class=\"flex items-start gap-3\"><div class=\"mt-0.5 shrink-0\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-5 w-5\"><path d=\"m21.73 18-8-14a2 2 0 0 0-3.48 0l-8 14A2 2 0 0 0 4 21h16a2 2 0 0 0 1.73-3Z\"/><path d=\"M12 9v4\"/><path d=\"M12 17h.01\"/></svg></div><div class=\"min-w-0 flex-1\"><p class=\"text-sm font-semibold\">Rule of thumb</p><div class=\"mt-1 text-sm\">Isolate unsafe behind a safe API. Document invariants.</div></div></div></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s20\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">20. Deployment</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>FROM rust:1.78 as build\nWORKDIR /src\nCOPY . .\nRUN cargo build --release\nFROM debian:bookworm-slim\nCOPY --from=build /src/target/release/myapp /myapp\nENTRYPOINT [&quot;/myapp&quot;]</code></pre></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"summary\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Summary &amp; Key Takeaways</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Rust's steep entry pays back in reliable, fast code. Master ownership; the rest of the language flows from it.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"faqs\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">FAQ</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>Which async runtime?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Tokio is the default for most work; smol/async-std for niches.</div></details>\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>ORM or sqlx?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">sqlx first. SeaORM/Diesel when you want abstractions.</div></details>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"glossary\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Glossary</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li><strong>Trait object</strong> — <code>dyn Trait</code>, dynamic dispatch.</li>\n          <li><strong>Lifetime</strong> — compile-time label of reference validity.</li>\n          <li><strong>Cargo</strong> — Rust's build tool and package manager.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"references\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">References</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\"><References /></div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"disclaimer\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Disclaimer</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Snapshot for study. Verify against current stable Rust.</p>\n      </div></section>"}